/-! # Full-support coherent structure direct image of a finite cover

Source: Stacks Project, Spaces Cohomology, Tag 0GF7,
`lemma-finite-morphism-Noetherian`, statement and proof
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-finite-cover-structure-support).

The cartesian square describes any realization of the specified fibre product.
Finiteness and closed immersion are representable scheme-test properties. Local
Noetherianity is tested on every etale scheme chart; coherence uses the existing
Zariski chart restriction, and support is the existing nonzero-geometric-germ locus.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace

/-- A finite surjective cover of a locally Noetherian algebraic space, after restriction
 to any closed subspace, has coherent structure direct image with full support.
Source: Stacks Project, Spaces Cohomology, Tag 0GF7,
`lemma-finite-morphism-Noetherian`, statement and proof
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-finite-cover-structure-support).

Proof:
1. The sheaf fibre product exists by lem-trf-space-fibre-products-etale-covers.
   Finiteness is stable under base change by lem-sfb-finite-space-morphism-topology.
   The point-image formula of lem-a1-space-point-open-calculus makes f' surjective.
   Scheme tests identify the base change of i' with that of i, so i' is closed.
2. Closed immersions are finite: A/I is generated by 1 over A. For a finite map
   H → B with B locally Noetherian, pull back Noetherian affine etale charts of B.
   Their sources are affine finite algebras and are Noetherian by
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-algebra-noetherian. Any other etale chart of H has an etale
   cover locally of finite type over these sources. Apply pqf-lem-locnoeth-lft and
   lem-trf-etale-local-noetherian-descent. Apply this to Y, Z, and then Z'.
3. On an etale chart U → Z, put V = Z' ×_Z U, finite over U. By
   lem-trf-space-enlarged-etale-ringed-site-model, direct image on any W → U has
   sections Γ(Z' ×_Z W, O). Hence restriction of G equals the etale structure
   direct image from V, respecting addition, scalars, and restrictions. This is
   the objectwise section identity and uses no proper or flat base-change theorem.
4. Apply lem-weil-pbc-finite-pushforward-coherent to V → U and O_V, then
   lem-trf-scheme-zariski-etale-quasi-coherent-equivalence. Its qc separated
   hypothesis holds: the map is affine, and its diagonal is given by the
   surjective multiplication B ⊗_A B → B. This proves coherence on every U.
   Local presentations (def-trf-space-quasi-coherent-module) give global
   quasi-coherence of G, so it is coherent in the stated chartwise sense.
5. If a geometric stalk of G vanished, its unit germ would vanish. The pointed
   neighbourhoods are cofiltered by lem-weil-pbc-pointed-etale-neighbourhoods-cofiltered;
   def-weil-pbc-geometric-stalks and lem-sc-filtered-colimit-map-zero give a pointed
   etale neighbourhood W where the unit is zero. Step 3 says 1 = 0 on Z' ×_Z W.
   This scheme is empty, since otherwise its nonzero local rings would have 1 = 0.
   But the point-image formula and surjectivity of f' make it surjective onto the
   nonempty pointed W, a contradiction. All geometric stalks are nonzero, proving
   full support. If Z is empty the support equality is vacuous. -/
theorem finiteCover_structure_coherent_support
    {S : Scheme.{u}} {X Y Z Z' : AlgebraicSpace S}
    (f : Y ⟶ X)
    (hf : IsRepresentableWith (fun _ _ p ↦ IsFinite p.left) f.hom.hom)
    (hs : pointImage f.hom.hom = Set.univ)
    (hln : ∀ T : X.EtaleSite, IsLocallyNoetherian (X.etaleForget.obj T))
    (i : Z ⟶ X)
    (hi : IsRepresentableWith (fun _ _ p ↦ IsClosedImmersion p.left) i.hom.hom)
    (i' : Z' ⟶ Y) (f' : Z' ⟶ Z)
    (hp : IsPullback i'.hom f'.hom f.hom i.hom) :
    IsRepresentableWith (fun _ _ p ↦ IsFinite p.left) f'.hom.hom ∧
    pointImage f'.hom.hom = Set.univ ∧
    IsRepresentableWith (fun _ _ p ↦ IsClosedImmersion p.left) i'.hom.hom ∧
    (∀ T : Y.EtaleSite, IsLocallyNoetherian (Y.etaleForget.obj T)) ∧
    (∀ T : Z.EtaleSite, IsLocallyNoetherian (Z.etaleForget.obj T)) ∧
    (∀ T : Z'.EtaleSite, IsLocallyNoetherian (Z'.etaleForget.obj T)) ∧
    ((moduleDirectImage f').obj (SheafOfModules.unit Z'.structureSheaf)).IsQuasicoherent ∧
    (∀ T : Z.EtaleSite,
      RingedSpace.IsCoherent (Z.etaleForget.obj T).toRingedSpace
        ((Z.schemeRestriction T).obj
          ((moduleDirectImage f').obj (SheafOfModules.unit Z'.structureSheaf)))) ∧
    moduleSupport ((moduleDirectImage f').obj (SheafOfModules.unit Z'.structureSheaf)) =
      Set.univ := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace
